Good to have you here! SportMeter was specifically developed for volunteer trainers, coaches and supervisors who want to notice a lot, but cannot pick up on everything themselves. Athletes answer short questions about how they are doing. You see the answers, attendance and points of attention in one place.

### Why is this relevant now?

Coaches and supervisors are getting more and more on their plate. You pay attention to training, attendance, motivation, recovery and group dynamics. And sometimes to tension, stress or social safety. But what you know is scattered: in WhatsApp groups, in a form, in a conversation after training or in the head of one trainer.

That makes it difficult to see who is participating well, who is dropping off and which themes keep coming back. With large teams, changing supervisors or multiple training sessions per week, you simply lose track of those things.

### How does it work?

SportMeter supports you throughout the season at three moments:

1. Before you start
- Prepare your questions. Link short questions to a training session, match or fixed weekly moment about, for example, energy, recovery, enjoyment, load, motivation or team spirit. Athletes see them at the right moment.
- Easily choose a focus for the week. For example, communication on the field, recovery, confidence or tension before the match. This way, everything is linked to one recognisable theme.
2. During the busy moments of the season
- See who has responded. No more chasing separate messages.
- Follow one athlete over time. In the profile, you see previous answers and whether something comes up more often.
- Get a signal from the team. Low response, an athlete with a support request, a new comment from another supervisor.
3. In the follow-up
- Record what you see. An observation after a training session or conversation is saved for the whole coaching team.
- Mark who needs attention. With a reason and with a moment when you close it again.
- Plan the follow-up conversation. With the athlete, the team or a fellow supervisor. This makes follow-up concrete, instead of something that “still needs to happen”.

Athletes share their answers with their coaches and supervisors and can keep notes private if they want to. Individual answers are only visible to the coaching team. Data is stored securely and never shared with third parties.

### Together for Enjoyment

The strength lies in simplicity and repetition. Athletes briefly share how they are doing; you see faster what needs attention, and the team follows up in a targeted way. As a result, coaching depends less on gut feeling, separate messages or chance conversations.

You do not have to do more. You simply see more clearly where your attention makes the biggest difference.

